  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Orange Corners: Palestine &#x2013; Business Angel Network</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth unemployment is one of the biggest challenges in the Palestinian Territories. According to the World Bank, the percentage of youth not in employment, education or training (NEET) combined in the West Bank and Gaza has increased from 27.5 percent in 2011 to 34.5 percent in 2020.In addition, The Palestinian Central Bureau of Statistics (PCBS) reports that 36 percent of youth graduates (19-29) in the West Bank is unemployed. Entrepreneurship has become an important mechanism to aid the creation of jobs.In the Palestinian Territories, several initiatives are taking place to train, mentor and coach entrepreneurs to setup and grow their business. However, a major roadblock for these starting entrepreneurs is access to finance. Political instability alongside restrictions, put in place as a result of the Israeli closure policy, have consequences for expected rates of return, the scalability of investments and limit financial transactions hampering growth.By supporting the development of a Business Angel Network, a gateway to early stage finance for young entrepreneurs will be established. Young entrepreneurs will have the ability to pitch their idea to vested investors. This will allow entrepreneurs to have access to early stage finance and mentorship.</narrative>
  </description>
